> Complete preserved experiment

The four original methods retain40000 steps per run,8 runs, seeds1..8, alpha.3, gamma.99, epsilon.1 and beta.02. Counts include resets and persist. Evaluation uses only task Q-values; novelty-augmented collection returns are not task performance. All objectives, policy improvements, optimizer steps, collection and evaluation loops remain editable below. Additional checkpoint writes consume no RNG draws. The native grid renderer records the seeded greedy rollouts.

```{cpp, results="output", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace report_capture {
inline dm::nn::NamedTensors arrays;
template<class T> void Save(const std::string& name,const std::vector<T>& values){arrays.push_back({name,dm::nn::from_vector(values)});}
inline void Table(const std::string& name,const dm::rl::foundations::QTable&q){arrays.push_back({name,q.tensor()});}
